# --- T8: the read API (handoff 003)
scope :: api.rs :: * :: the API's prefixes, the description's path and the media types: addresses and media types, no sentence
scope :: problem.rs :: * :: the registry of problem codes: stable identifiers, the form of the URN and the standard's member names; every sentence a problem says is a catalog message chosen by `Code::keys` (the tests in problem/tests.rs hold that)
scope :: reply.rs :: * :: media types and the `Link` header's fixed value; no sentence
scope :: endpoints.rs :: * :: the JSON member names of the answers, the registry's public reasons (written for the reviewer of the route table), the names of query parameters and an operator's log line; every sentence a caller reads is a problem detail in problem.rs
scope :: describe.rs :: * :: the OpenAPI document's descriptions: English by decision, the reference a programmer reads (like an operator's log line); the problem details a caller gets are catalog messages in the caller's language
scope :: openapi.rs :: * :: the OpenAPI document's structure and descriptions: English by decision, like describe.rs; machine-readable member names
scope :: across.rs :: * :: the endpoints of the links, health, search and changes: JSON member names and the codes of the answers (kinds, actions, marks); every sentence a caller reads is a problem detail or a catalog message chosen by the pages' own functions
scope :: past.rs :: * :: the endpoints of a page's past: JSON member names and codes (statuses, kinds); every sentence a caller reads is a problem detail or a catalog message chosen by the pages' own functions
scope :: shape.rs :: * :: the JSON shapes the endpoints share: member names and codes (person kinds, events, line kinds); the sentences in them are the pages' own catalog messages
scope :: shapes.rs :: * :: the OpenAPI schemas of the answers: English descriptions by decision, like describe.rs; machine-readable member names
# --- T7: the write API (handoff 004)
scope :: write.rs :: * :: the write API's shared start and finish, and its descriptions (English by decision, like describe.rs): header names, media types, the order of the checks in prose; every sentence a caller reads is a problem detail in problem.rs
scope :: base.rs :: * :: the form of the proposal revision's ETag, the names of the members a stale base carries and the header names; no sentence a reader sees
scope :: body.rs :: * :: the strict reading of a write's JSON body: the names of the members it takes; every refusal is the problem `invalid-body`, a catalog message
scope :: refuse.rs :: * :: the stable words of what a refusal names (`summary-missing`, `at`, `never`, ...) and the members that carry the numbers of a limit; every sentence is a catalog message or the pages' own words
scope :: files.rs :: * :: the pages of a proposal sent as JSON: member names and the stable words of what was wrong with a page; every sentence is a catalog message the form uses as well
scope :: answer.rs :: * :: the JSON member names of a proposal as the write API tells it; no sentence a reader sees
scope :: propose.rs :: * :: the write API's proposals: JSON member names and the operator's log lines (English by decision: operator vocabulary); every sentence a caller reads is a problem detail
scope :: decide.rs :: * :: the write API's review: JSON member names, the words of an acceptance's outcome (`signed`, `already-signed`) and the feature a build lacks; every sentence a caller reads is a problem detail
scope :: writes.rs :: * :: the OpenAPI schemas of the write API: English descriptions by decision, like describe.rs; machine-readable member names
